text\"></span></span>.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":3}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-08-academic-listening-test-1-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c8-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3170393-cambridge-ielts-08-academic-listening-test-1-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c8-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"diagram_labelling","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Geography</strong></p><p><b>Studying geography helps us to understand:</b></p><ul><li>the effects of different processes on the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the Earth</li><li>the dynamic between <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and population</li></ul><p><b>Two main branches of study:</b></p><ul><li>physical features</li><li>human lifestyles and their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><b>Specific study areas:</b> biophysical, topographic, political, social, economic, historical and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> geography, and also cartography</p><p><b>Key point:</b> geography helps us to understand our surroundings and the associated <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p><b>What do geographers do?</b></p><ul><li>find data – e.g. conduct censuses, collect information in the form of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> using computer and satellite technology</li><li>analyse data – identify <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, e.g. cause and effect</li><li>publish findings in form of:a) maps\n<ul><li>easy to carry</li><li>can show physical features of large and small areas</li><li>BUT a two-dimensional map will always have some <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p>b) aerial photos</p><ul><li>can show vegetation problems, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> density, ocean floor etc.</li></ul><p>c) Landsat pictures sent to receiving stations</p><ul><li>used for monitoring <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> conditions etc.</li></ul></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-08-academic-listening-test-1-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c8-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-c8-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c8-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"multiple_choice","ieltsQuestionType":"multiple_choice_single","question_text":"","correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_variants":["C"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3165711_1","order_index":1,"points":1,"sourceOptions":[{"value":"A","text":"Aa group playing music."},{"value":"B","text":"Ba display of instruments."},{"value":"C","text":"Ca video about the festival."}]},{"id":"en-c8-t1-l-q2","part_id":"en-c8-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c8-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"multiple_choice","ieltsQuestionType":"multiple_choice_single","question_text":"","correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_variants":["B"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3165711_2","order_index":2,"points":1,"sourceOptions":[{"value":"A","text":"Asee well."},{"value":"B","text":"Bhear clearly."},{"value":"C","text":"Cpay less."}]},{"id":"en-c8-t1-l-q3","part_id":"en-c8-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c8-t1-l-g1-1","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"48 North Avenue","correct_answer_variants":["48 North Avenue"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3165712_1","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c8-t1-l-q4","part_id":"en-c8-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c8-t1-l-g1-1","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"